# WHAT THE BUILDER DOES NOT NEED TO CARRY.
#
# THE PROBLEM. This repo tracks 2.1 GB of files and had no ignore file
# of any kind, so every deploy shipped all 2.1 GB to the builder and
# baked it into the image. Nixpacks does `COPY . .`; there is nothing
# in that step that knows a 660 MB directory of finished research
# artifacts has no bearing on `python research_service.py`. The cost is
# paid twice -- once uploading and layering the context, and again on
# every deploy pulling the resulting image.
#
# THE RULE APPLIED HERE. A path is excluded only if NOTHING the running
# services open can reach it. That was checked rather than assumed:
# every literal `research/...` and `data/...` path in research_service.py,
# researcher/*.py and bot/*.py was grepped, and each directory below has
# zero readers.
#
# WHAT DELIBERATELY STAYS, because the searcher genuinely reads it:
#
#     data/polygon/          286 MB   tier 1, 10 markets of 5-min bars
#     data/research_bars/     19 MB   precomputed tier-2 bars
#     data/depth/             26 MB   tier 3, the NQ book
#     data/research_data/     81 MB   COT / FRED / DTS, read by context.py
#
# That is ~410 MB the service cannot run without, and it is not touched.

# Finished mining artifacts. 661 MB of .npz feature caches and result
# tables from the 2026-07-31 campaign. Offline research output; no
# runtime reader anywhere in the repo.
research/mining_2026_07_31/mega2/

# Old feature-search checkpoints, 497 MB. Zero references in any module.
data/fsearch_ck/

# Pulse checkpoints, 116 MB. Zero references in any module.
data/pulse_ck_*.pkl

# Never useful in an image.
.git/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
*.ipynb_checkpoints/
